---
description: ClearBed project rules that apply to every change
alwaysApply: true
---

Project: ClearBed — a discharge-barrier prediction and placement copilot for hospital case managers.

Stack (do not substitute without asking):
- Python 3.11, uv for deps, ruff + mypy, pytest
- DuckDB as the local warehouse; dbt-core + dbt-duckdb (keep a commented Snowflake profile)
- LightGBM, scikit-learn, SHAP, MLflow (local file store)
- LangGraph + LangChain, ChromaDB, sentence-transformers (all-MiniLM-L6-v2)
- LLM via a provider abstraction: "ollama" (default, local), "bedrock", "groq"
- FastAPI backend, Streamlit frontend, Docker Compose

Hard rules:
- All patient data is SYNTHETIC (Synthea) unless a config flag says otherwise. Never log full patient records.
- The Groq provider must refuse to run when DATA_MODE != "synthetic" (PHI safety). Only bedrock/ollama are allowed for real data.
- Config lives in `src/clearbed/config.py` (pydantic-settings, .env). No hard-coded paths or keys.
- Every module gets type hints, docstrings, and at least one pytest test.
- Agent actions that leave the system (sending a referral) require human approval. Never auto-send.
- Prefer small, composable functions. No notebooks in src/.
- When unsure about an external dataset's column names, write code that inspects and maps headers instead of hard-coding them.
- Keep README.md updated with every step that adds a command.
